; 128K: page in bank A
;
; Writes A to the 128K paging port and remembers it in #R$8507. BC is saved and restored.
;
; Hardware: writes port $7FFD (nothing happens on a 48K Spectrum).
;
; A Value for port $7FFD (bits 0-2 RAM bank at $C000, bit 4 ROM)
@label=PageInBank
c$85CA PUSH BC
@isub=LD BC,PAGING_PORT
 $85CB LD BC,$7FFD
 $85CE LD ($8507),A         ; last value written, for #R$85D5
 $85D1 OUT (C),A
 $85D3 POP BC
 $85D4 RET
